>
>Peyote is a pretty smart dog.
>
>Someone please reply and tell me that this assumption [about 
>conciousness] is NOT basic to this list.  I don't think it is necessarily 
>wrong, but I have a very good 
>grounding in this subject, and have read incredibly persuasive works both 
>pro and con.  I don't think this can be simply assumed.

This assumptions is definitely NOT basic to this list.  I do not speak for
anyone but myself, but I've been on the list for some time and have seen all
sorts of things proposed.  And as for myself, I am quite comfortable with my
belief that consciousness in humans is an extension of consciousness in
insects, fish, and your dog Peyote (though let's not forget that they're
our cousins, not our ancestors, and may have taken a somewhat different
route in cognitive complexification - especially the insects).

